IPv4 uses 32-bit addresses.

# Example
192 . 168 . 1 . 25
 \     \    \    \
 8     8    8    8 bits

8 + 8 + 8 + 8 = 32 bits

They're normally written as four decimal numbers separated by periods:
192.168.1.25

# Examples of IP Addresses
| Address        | Meaning                                                |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| `127.0.0.1`    | Localhost                                              |
| `192.168.1.1`  | Common private router address                          |
| `192.168.1.25` | Example private device                                 |
| `10.0.0.5`     | Private network address                                |
| `172.16.0.10`  | Private network address                                |
| `8.8.8.8`      | Public DNS address operated by Google                  |
| `0.0.0.0`      | Unspecified / all IPv4 interfaces depending on context |

